# LICENSE — AstrologAsStar

AstrologAsStar is a **derivative work** of the classic **Astrolog32** program
(itself a line of Astrolog 5.40 / 5.41g by Walter D. Pullen with later
modifications, plus portions originating from Astrolog 6.00 and beyond).
It was refactored from the source of the "A32_V3_51" Chinese-customized build
into a GUI-free, cross-platform C++11 engine + static library + CLI.

Because the source tree mixes code of **different upstream origins**, a single
one-line license cannot truthfully cover the whole repository. This file
therefore states the effective license by origin, in descending order of
restriction. When any doubt exists, the more restrictive license applies to
the file/portion in question.

## 1. Code inherited from Astrolog 5.40 / 5.41g (Walter D. Pullen lineage)

The original file headers (kept in `astroproject/src/*.cpp`,
`astroproject/include/**` and `astroproject/include/models/version.h`) state,
and continue to apply:

> The graphics database and chart display routines used in this program are
> Copyright (C) 1991-1998 by Walter D. Pullen. Permission is granted to freely
> use and distribute these routines provided one doesn't sell, restrict, or
> profit from them in any way. Modification is allowed provided these notices
> remain with any altered or edited versions of the program.
>
> The main planetary calculation routines are a conversion to C of routines
> created by James Neely as listed in Michael Erlewine's 'Manual of Computer
> Programming for Astrologers' (Matrix Software). The copyright grants
> permission for personal use but not to sell or profit from them.
>
> This copyright notice must not be changed or removed by any user of this
> program.

These terms cover all engine logic, tables, and data inherited from that
lineage (most of `astrolog.cpp`-derived charting, aspects, dignities,
listing/printing routines, and the corresponding headers).

## 2. Code from Astrolog 6.00 and beyond (GNU GPL)

Portions of the code (including the `CI`/`IS`/`US`/`CP` data model and the
`CastChart`/`ProcessInput` computation core migrated from Astrolog 6.00+,
as stated in the retained file headers) are licensed under the
**GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later
version** — see <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html>.

The **aggregate library and binaries of this project are distributed under
GPL-2.0-or-later**, because they link GPL-licensed portions together with the
rest of the engine. Newly written portions (section 3) are offered under the
same GPL terms when used as part of this aggregate, and additionally under MIT
when extracted and used standalone outside of this project.

